+Account rotation is evaluated only when Core admits a new root user turn. It never changes an active turn, replays a prompt, or fails over after execution starts. A successful manual account switch pins the selected slot as the fixed target; an automatic selection preserves the rotation mode and commits its cursor only after the turn starts. Creating, replacing, or reauthenticating a slot removes it from every automatic membership before credentials are changed, while preserving any fixed target. Clients can add it back explicitly without restarting the TUI or app-server.
